{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nCodex currently has no Serena MCP entry, while this project relies on Serena/Pyright for semantic navigation. The tracked `.claude/settings.json` does not configure MCP servers. Separately, this operator machine's untracked Claude project config (`~/.claude.json`) launches Serena via `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena`; that machine-local fact was inspected only to identify the existing server. The delivery design is independently grounded: the current Codex manual supports project-scoped MCP servers in trusted `.codex/config.toml`, and Serena 1.6.2.dev0 exposes a `codex` context plus `--project-from-cwd` specifically for CLI agents/worktrees.\n\n## Verified inputs\n- `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena serena -V` returned `Serena 1.6.2.dev0`.\n- `git ls-remote https://github.com/oraios/serena.git HEAD` returned `c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e`.\n- `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena@c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e serena start-mcp-server --help` succeeded and documented `--context` plus `--project-from-cwd`.\n- `codex mcp list` in the current worktree confirms no `serena` entry exists before the change.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a project-scoped `mcp_servers.serena` STDIO entry to `.codex/config.toml`; project scope is intentional so every contributor/worktree gets the repo-required semantic navigation server after trusting the repo, without mutating each operator's global config.\n- Launch the same Serena distribution currently used on this machine, but pin the verified upstream commit: `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena@c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e`.\n- Pass `serena start-mcp-server --context codex --project-from-cwd` so each checkout/worktree activates itself; commit no user-specific project path.\n- Set `startup_timeout_sec = 120` to bound and accommodate a cold uvx resolution. Keep `required` unset/false so a Serena startup failure is reported by Codex without preventing all Codex work.\n- Validate TOML with Python 3.11+ `tomllib`; run `codex mcp list` from the isolated worktree and require an enabled `serena` row containing the pinned command/args; run the pinned `serena start-mcp-server --help` command and an MCP initialize/list-tools smoke test from the worktree, bounded by a test harness timeout.\n- Negative control: run `codex mcp list` from a temporary untrusted/non-rebar directory and confirm the project-scoped server is not injected there.\n- Land the single-file config change through Gerrit with DCO and the ticket trailer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `codex mcp list` from a trusted rebar worktree discovers an enabled `serena` STDIO server from `.codex/config.toml`, using the pinned upstream commit.\n- [ ] The server argv uses Serena's `codex` context and `--project-from-cwd`; no user-specific rebar path is committed.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import tomllib; tomllib.load(open('.codex/config.toml', 'rb'))\"`, the pinned Serena CLI smoke command, and an MCP initialize/list-tools smoke test all succeed.\n- [ ] `codex mcp list` outside the trusted rebar project does not expose the project-scoped `serena` entry; Serena startup remains non-required so failure does not block Codex itself.\n- [ ] The config diff contains no secrets, and `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default suite remain green; a same-base full-gate result may be reused because this task changes only static Codex configuration.\n\n## References\nCurrent Codex manual: trusted projects may scope MCP servers in `.codex/config.toml`; STDIO entries accept `command`, `args`, `cwd`, `startup_timeout_sec`, and optional `required`. Serena CLI help at the pinned commit documents `--context codex` and `--project-from-cwd`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785619908696287001,"uuid":"852668f6-6db2-4c53-a4b3-7b6492646a53"}